  "enhanced_information": "The patient presents with a resting tremor of the right hand, which decreases with movement, and reduced arm swing while walking, all of which are characteristic of Parkinson's disease. The family history of a movement disorder further supports this diagnosis. Levodopa/carbidopa is the first-line pharmacotherapy for Parkinson's disease, as it effectively addresses the motor symptoms associated with the condition. Other options, such as donepezil (used for Alzheimer's), trihexyphenidyl (an anticholinergic for tremors), clonazepam (an anxiolytic), and propranolol (for essential tremor), are not appropriate for this patient's presentation. Therefore, the most appropriate pharmacotherapy is Levodopa/carbidopa."
